@startuml
title UC-06 · Serve Packages (Upload side of a UC-02 transfer)
 
participant "Requesting Daemon\n(remote peer's machine,\nrunning its own UC-02)" as RemotePeer
participant "Serving Daemon\n(THIS machine)" as Daemon
participant "pkg cache\n(/var/cache/pkg, read-only)" as Cache
participant Tracker
 
note over RemotePeer, Daemon : Same transfer as UC-02's fetch loop,\nseen from the uploader's side.\npkg is NOT involved anywhere here —\nthis is daemon-to-daemon traffic.\nWire: docs/peer-transfer-spec-v0.2.md

RemotePeer -> Daemon: GET /pkg/packageName-version
activate Daemon
note right of Daemon : An ordinary HTTP server on the port\nannounced to the tracker as servingPort.\nThe namespace is deliberately NOT the\nfacade's .../All/name-version.pkg —\na seeding daemon must not be a\nsyntactically valid pkg mirror.

Daemon -> Daemon : validateRequest()
note right : Network input from an UNTRUSTED\nremote daemon — not user input,\nso not pkg's job. Malformed or\nhostile requests must be rejected\nwithout crashing. The fuzz target is\nthis HTTP surface end to end: arbitrary\nbytes in, never a panic. Request framing\nitself is now the stdlib's job.

Daemon -> Cache: open(packageName-version)
activate Cache

alt package exists locally
Cache --> Daemon: open file handle + size
deactivate Cache
Daemon --> RemotePeer: 200, Content-Length, streamed body
note over Daemon, RemotePeer: Served from an open file, not a byte\nslice, so the sender is constant-memory\ntoo. NO hash is computed here — the\nrequester verifies end to end (UC-02).
RemotePeer --> Daemon : transfer complete

else package not found
Cache --> Daemon: notFound
deactivate Cache
Daemon --> RemotePeer: 404 (package not held)
Daemon -> Tracker: announce(fullPackageList)
note right : Full re-announce (UC-05):\nif one entry drifted, others\nmay have too (e.g. pkg clean).\nDaemon never serves data\nit does not hold.
end
 
deactivate Daemon
@enduml

